{"tool_name":"neatms","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"neatms","identifiers":[],"license":"MIT","summary":"Neatms is an open source python package for untargeted lcms signal labelling and filtering","home_url":"https://github.com/bihealth/NeatMS","keywords":[],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":4},"biotools":{"id":"neatms","home":"https://anaconda.org/bioconda/neatms","license":"MIT","summary":"NeatMS is an open source python package for untargeted LCMS signal labelling and filtering. NeatMS enables automated filtering of false positive MS peaks reported by commonly used LCMS data processing pipelines. NeatMS relies on neural network based classification.","addition_date":"2022-07-06T15:00:55.171504Z","last_update_date":"2025-11-03T16:32:44.163513Z","tool_type":["Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:neatms","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"dieter.beule@bih-charite.de","name":"Dieter Beule","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Jennifer A. Kirwan"},{"name":"Yoann Gloaguen","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0493-8592"}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://neatms.readthedocs.io/en/latest/"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["recetox-specdatri"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Filtering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3695"},{"term":"Network analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3927"},{"term":"Peak detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3215"}]}],"name":"NeatMS","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1021/ACS.ANALCHEM.1C02220","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2022 American Chemical Society. All rights reserved.Available automated methods for peak detection in untargeted metabolomics suffer from poor precision. We present NeatMS, which uses machine learning based on a convoluted neural network to reduce the number and fraction of false peaks. NeatMS comes with a pre-trained model representing expert knowledge in the differentiation of true chemical signal from noise. Furthermore, it provides all necessary functions to easily train new models or improve existing ones by transfer learning. Thus, the tool improves peak curation and contributes to the robust and scalable analysis of large-scale experiments. We show how to integrate it into different liquid chromatography-mass spectrometry (LC-MS) analysis workflows, quantify its performance, and compare it to various other approaches. NeatMS software is available as open source on github under permissive MIT license and is also provided as easy-to-install PyPi and Bioconda packages.","authors":[{"name":"Beule D."},{"name":"Gloaguen Y."},{"name":"Kirwan J.A."}],"date":"2022-03-29T00:00:00Z","journal":"Analytical Chemistry","title":"Deep Learning-Assisted Peak Curation for Large-Scale LC-MS Metabolomics"},"pmcid":"PMC8969107","pmid":"35290737"}],"topic":[{"term":"Machine learning","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3474"},{"term":"Metabolomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3172"},{"term":"Proteomics experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3520"},{"term":"Workflows","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0769"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"NeatMS","home":"https://bio.tools/neatms","license":"MIT","summary":"NeatMS is an open source python package for untargeted LCMS signal labelling and filtering. NeatMS enables automated filtering of false positive MS peaks reported by commonly used LCMS data processing pipelines. NeatMS relies on neural network based classification.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:neatms/lib/anaconda.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true,"repository":{}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentatio